                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5aa9a7ef-28ee-47f0-adc2-c577cb589daa",
                        "source_entry_id": "9fb5f2e2-026a-3a33-838e-eb65c04190ed",
                        "source_sense_id": "bdd3a91f-e496-3a15-9100-3e7c3684dd8f",
                        "target_lang_word": "Cold War",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Cold War",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "be3d33d9-6e3e-33c2-89ee-57b41019a17e",
                                        "entry_id": "1092a956-e496-31b2-84cf-31fd763e455f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The period of hostility short of open war between the Soviet Bloc and the Western powers, especially the United States, between 1945 and 1991."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1350c1c2-650e-4f0f-8909-d62de4f27659",
                                                "sense_id": "be3d33d9-6e3e-33c2-89ee-57b41019a17e",
                                                "text": "Well Russia at the present time is at a crossroads. It is often said that the Cold War is over and that the West has won it- that's only half true. Because what has happened is that the communists have been defeated, but the ideas of freedom now are on trial. If they don't work, there will be a reversion to, not communism which has failed, but what I call a new despotism which would pose a mortal danger to the rest of the world because it would be infected with the virus of Russian imperialism which of course has been a characteristic of Russian foreign policy for centuries."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "386d8a8a-b24a-4931-9186-c9d3de948bdb",
                                                "sense_id": "be3d33d9-6e3e-33c2-89ee-57b41019a17e",
                                                "text": "The situation in Berlin had its uses for Moscow, of course, as for others–the city had become the primary listening post and spy center of the Cold War; some 70 different agencies were operating there by 1961, and it was in Berlin that Soviet espionage scored some of their greatest successes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f0b3d7e-55c3-4068-b820-d55f44fd7567",
                                                "sense_id": "be3d33d9-6e3e-33c2-89ee-57b41019a17e",
                                                "text": "The dynamic tests at Wildenrath use continuous test tracks built on the site of a former Royal Air Force station that was vacated after the end of the Cold War."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
